5
00:12.160 --> 00:17.440
[Your Third Series]

6
00:17.940 --> 00:18.860
Thank you

7
00:19.540 --> 00:20.620
for choosing me.

8
00:27.120 --> 00:28.560
Sarm...

9
00:28.870 --> 00:30.170
So good.

10
00:34.200 --> 00:35.000
Thank you

11
00:35.560 --> 00:37.240
for moving in with me completely.

12
00:37.990 --> 00:40.430
Your house is also mine.

13
00:53.560 --> 00:54.760
Two plates of steak, please.

14
00:55.860 --> 00:56.620
Thank you.

15
01:10.900 --> 01:11.740
Payu.

16
01:14.210 --> 01:15.400
Did I keep you waiting?

17
01:15.580 --> 01:17.220
- It's only been 5 minutes. - Thank you.

18
01:22.020 --> 01:22.900
Well...

19
01:23.500 --> 01:24.700
You asked me to come here.

20
01:24.820 --> 01:25.940
Is there something you need?

21
01:27.700 --> 01:28.500
Of course.

22
01:31.190 --> 01:32.190
I missed you.

23
01:34.220 --> 01:36.180
You just wanted to flirt with me?

24
01:36.560 --> 01:38.200
Hey, what makes you say that?

25
01:38.289 --> 01:40.289
You rarely have time for me at all.

26
01:40.860 --> 01:42.200
If I don't give you a reason to come,

27
01:42.220 --> 01:43.340
I'll never get to meet you.

28
01:46.620 --> 01:47.860
- Thank you. - Thank you very much.

29
01:48.620 --> 01:49.440
Wow...

30
01:49.460 --> 01:50.500
I'll help.

31
01:51.340 --> 01:53.240
This looks so good. You ordered it for me?

32
01:53.259 --> 01:54.860
Yeah. It's your favorite, isn't it?

33
01:57.700 --> 01:59.259
How are things lately?

34
02:00.700 --> 02:02.020
Lately?

35
02:02.200 --> 02:04.000
It's been...so-so, actually.

36
02:04.290 --> 02:07.020
The farm is back to normal once again, too.

37
02:09.620 --> 02:11.140
The Adisuan Family

38
02:11.780 --> 02:12.850
is a strange one, isn't it?

39
02:13.980 --> 02:14.740
Strange...?

40
02:15.780 --> 02:16.860
How exactly?

41
02:17.100 --> 02:19.579
Back then, I thought...

42
02:20.020 --> 02:21.780
no one in the family would get married.

43
02:23.260 --> 02:24.180
What about now?

44
02:25.060 --> 02:27.020
Sib and PiMai got married.

45
02:27.500 --> 02:28.220
Mm.

46
02:28.690 --> 02:30.370
The same goes for Namnueng.

47
02:31.079 --> 02:33.120
Sarm and Jam also just got married.

48
02:33.360 --> 02:34.020
Mm.

49
02:35.620 --> 02:36.780
But there are...

50
02:38.020 --> 02:39.180
two people left.

51
02:42.940 --> 02:44.140
Two...?

52
02:44.980 --> 02:46.500
Who? I have no idea.

53
02:49.100 --> 02:50.060
- Uh... - Oh...

54
02:50.380 --> 02:52.579
You mean Wasin and Lantao, right?

55
02:52.900 --> 02:54.220
Yeah, I've been

56
02:54.540 --> 02:55.880
snooping around actually.

57
02:55.900 --> 02:57.200
They've been hitting on each other,

58
02:57.220 --> 02:58.500
but no one knows when they'll get married.

59
02:59.700 --> 03:00.740
Yes, yes...

60
03:02.160 --> 03:04.610
Yes, you are correct. They've been seeing each other.

61
03:05.060 --> 03:05.860
But...

62
03:06.820 --> 03:08.140
I meant...

63
03:08.500 --> 03:09.500
A different pair.

64
03:14.300 --> 03:15.620
A different pair? I have no clue.

65
03:15.940 --> 03:17.300
I can see right through you, Doctor.

66
03:21.900 --> 03:23.060
I'm serious, you know?

67
03:25.800 --> 03:28.540
Seeing others starting their own families,

68
03:28.800 --> 03:30.100
I can't help feeling like...

69
03:30.900 --> 03:32.260
If there's someone...

70
03:32.700 --> 03:34.820
to have dinner with every day,

71
03:35.660 --> 03:36.700
that would be nice.

72
03:39.340 --> 03:41.579
You're good at flirting, Director.

73
03:42.280 --> 03:43.280
I'm not trying to flirt.

74
03:44.420 --> 03:47.020
I'm just planning ahead for when the project is wrapped up.

75
03:51.160 --> 03:52.300
Oh, Payu.

76
03:52.579 --> 03:54.380
Always comparing everything to films,

77
03:54.940 --> 03:55.960
you've never changed.

78
03:57.060 --> 03:58.660
I need to prepare a proper script

79
03:59.660 --> 04:01.020
just in case I get to shoot...

80
04:02.380 --> 04:03.660
my own wedding.

81
04:06.060 --> 04:07.200
Your wedding?

82
04:09.880 --> 04:11.060
Who would...

83
04:11.620 --> 04:13.340
your acting partner be? I don't know.

84
04:16.420 --> 04:17.260
You do know.

85
04:29.540 --> 04:30.540
If I asked you,

86
04:33.100 --> 04:34.100
would you accept?

87
04:38.140 --> 04:38.980
Gosh.

88
04:39.360 --> 04:40.240
Payu.

89
04:40.620 --> 04:42.020
You're asking me so suddenly.

90
04:42.110 --> 04:43.770
How could I be ready to give you an answer?

91
04:44.820 --> 04:45.980
I'll wait, then.

92
04:49.980 --> 04:50.980
You will?

93
04:52.540 --> 04:53.380
It's gonna take a long time.

94
04:57.120 --> 04:58.220
I could wait for you my whole life.

95
05:11.900 --> 05:12.940
What does this mean?

96
05:14.370 --> 05:15.780
It doesn't mean anything.

97
05:16.980 --> 05:18.380
You reached for my hand first, no?

98
05:21.580 --> 05:23.740
Oh, dig in already. The food's getting cold.

99
05:24.780 --> 05:26.020
Okay. I'll dig in, then.

100
05:26.620 --> 05:28.740
How will you eat if you don't let go?

101
05:29.380 --> 05:31.100
- Okay, okay. - The steak's getting cold.

102
05:35.940 --> 05:36.980
That's a big bite.

103
05:37.060 --> 05:37.940
This is a normal bite for me.

104
05:39.440 --> 05:41.020
That's such a tiny bite.

105
05:42.020 --> 05:43.120
- I'm shy. - Payu, are you pretending?

106
05:43.140 --> 05:44.159
I'm shy, you see.

107
05:44.180 --> 05:46.700
Usually, you'd just...wolf it down.

108
05:49.260 --> 05:50.500
You're talking too much.

