[Your Third Series]

145
07:43.590 --> 07:45.490
Babe,

146
07:52.650 --> 07:53.730
I missed you.

147
07:56.170 --> 07:57.310
Chubby Piglet.

148
07:57.330 --> 07:59.030
Clingy, hm?

149
08:02.110 --> 08:03.730
Are you hungry, Chubby Babe?

150
08:04.810 --> 08:06.770
This is your favorite, Chubby.

151
08:07.170 --> 08:09.690
Oh, egg-wrapped pad thai!

152
08:10.010 --> 08:11.610
You said you wanted to eat it last night.

153
08:13.170 --> 08:15.890
Sarm, you are always so sweet.

154
08:16.290 --> 08:17.650
Sure, I'm sweet.

155
08:17.830 --> 08:18.530
So...

156
08:18.690 --> 08:20.290
Do you love me?

157
08:21.850 --> 08:22.370
Hm?

158
08:38.770 --> 08:42.409
Sometimes, actions alone are not enough, do you know?

159
08:43.370 --> 08:44.410
If that's so,

160
08:44.610 --> 08:45.410
tonight

161
08:46.210 --> 08:47.490
you'll have to say things to me.

162
08:55.410 --> 08:56.010
Hey.

163
08:56.450 --> 08:57.150
Hm?

164
08:57.170 --> 08:58.490
I peeled some pomelos for you.

165
08:58.730 --> 09:00.090
Whoa...

166
09:00.690 --> 09:03.430
You are the sweetest man ever, Sarm.

167
09:03.450 --> 09:05.250
Of course.

168
09:14.610 --> 09:16.490
Oh, Little Jam, tonight,

169
09:16.770 --> 09:18.130
there'll be ghosts all over the farm.

170
09:18.910 --> 09:19.730
Are you scared, Chubby?

171
09:21.810 --> 09:24.330
- You mean the ghosts at the party tonight? - Mm.

172
09:24.930 --> 09:25.890
I am not scared.

173
09:26.190 --> 09:29.650
That is because I am protected by a pervert ghost every day.

174
09:30.450 --> 09:31.210
A pervert ghost?

175
09:31.390 --> 09:32.330
Who is it?

176
09:33.010 --> 09:34.650
Who is this pervert ghost?

177
09:36.490 --> 09:37.050
Huh?

178
09:42.610 --> 09:43.310
Hey.

179
09:43.330 --> 09:45.730
How was work today,

180
09:45.930 --> 09:46.810
Boss?

181
09:48.730 --> 09:50.090
It was fun.

182
09:53.020 --> 09:53.970
Oh.

183
09:55.280 --> 09:57.920
Someone was trying to flirt with me today.

184
10:00.170 --> 10:01.030
Who...?

185
10:01.570 --> 10:02.370
Who was it?

186
10:03.490 --> 10:03.970
Huh?

187
10:04.330 --> 10:05.370
You want to find out?

188
10:05.390 --> 10:06.090
Uh-huh.

189
10:09.930 --> 10:12.730
- That person probably works in the QC Department... - QC...

190
10:14.970 --> 10:16.310
The name is "Toi-ting."

191
10:16.330 --> 10:17.250
"Toi-ting."

192
10:19.750 --> 10:20.690
What did you say?

193
10:23.210 --> 10:25.090
I said...

194
10:25.970 --> 10:26.750
You said...?

195
10:28.230 --> 10:29.690
"I already have a spouse,

196
10:31.610 --> 10:33.490
and he is scary.

197
10:36.250 --> 10:39.210
He can kick a can from here and send it flying to Khon Kaen.

198
10:40.090 --> 10:42.850
He can even knock down a banana tree in one kick."

199
10:43.770 --> 10:44.850
Knock down a banana tree?

200
10:44.870 --> 10:46.470
It was you who got knocked down by me.

201
10:46.490 --> 10:47.810
Aww...that hurt.

202
10:51.210 --> 10:52.290
I changed my mind for today, then.

203
10:54.690 --> 10:55.490
Tonight,

204
10:55.970 --> 10:57.290
we're going to the party.

205
10:58.490 --> 10:59.330
The night of spirits

206
10:59.890 --> 11:01.210
only happens once a year.

207
11:01.650 --> 11:02.400
Right?

208
11:06.330 --> 11:08.370
Or are you going to be there to watch over me?

209
11:10.290 --> 11:11.250
It's called

210
11:11.410 --> 11:13.250
"showing off my spouse" at a party.

211
11:13.530 --> 11:14.170
Please?

212
11:16.770 --> 11:17.850
Yes, Chubby!

213
11:24.650 --> 11:27.050
Hug. Give me a hug, Chubby. - Whoa, you're strong.

214
11:27.130 --> 11:28.010
Hugging Chubby.

215
11:55.370 --> 11:55.970
Whoa!

216
11:59.010 --> 11:59.610
Hey.

217
12:00.170 --> 12:01.650
No matter what festival it is,

218
12:01.810 --> 12:02.610
whether it's New Year,

219
12:02.630 --> 12:03.570
Lunar New Year,

220
12:03.590 --> 12:04.570
Buddhist Lent Day,

221
12:04.810 --> 12:06.030
Songkran Day,

222
12:06.050 --> 12:07.010
or Loy Krathong,

223
12:07.290 --> 12:08.490
the themes are always related to ghosts.

224
12:10.060 --> 12:11.300
Who came up with it?

225
12:12.050 --> 12:14.210
I came up with it.

226
12:15.930 --> 12:17.170
Oh.

227
12:17.230 --> 12:18.410
It's such a brilliant idea, I was gonna say.

228
12:18.470 --> 12:20.750
There are over a thousand kinds of ghosts, right?

229
12:20.770 --> 12:22.410
That's why it's such a flexible theme.

230
12:22.930 --> 12:23.810
Amazing job.

231
12:24.010 --> 12:25.330
Keeping it consistent.

232
12:25.930 --> 12:26.530
Great.

233
12:31.330 --> 12:32.130
Sarm.

234
12:33.330 --> 12:35.690
I thought you'd dress up in a funny costume again.

235
12:36.090 --> 12:37.210
Jam.

236
12:39.530 --> 12:41.770
Finally, you're living a peaceful life.

237
12:44.390 --> 12:45.250
Hands off.

238
12:45.530 --> 12:47.050
What?

239
12:47.410 --> 12:48.850
Can I be handsome for once?

240
12:49.550 --> 12:50.570
Is there a problem?

241
12:51.250 --> 12:52.410
Oh...

242
12:53.210 --> 12:54.630
Very strict and serious.

243
12:59.410 --> 13:01.290
Smile, please.

244
13:03.470 --> 13:05.150
I'm just staying in the character

245
13:05.170 --> 13:06.490
of the calm and collected Dracula.

246
13:09.070 --> 13:11.370
But actually, I'm already smiling inside.

247
13:12.070 --> 13:12.690
Yes.

248
13:13.730 --> 13:15.050
Mr. Sarm, please come this way.

249
13:15.330 --> 13:16.090
I have to go.

250
13:16.490 --> 13:17.970
Don't be messing around anywhere, okay?

251
13:18.430 --> 13:20.410
I'll take care of Jam myself.

252
13:21.730 --> 13:22.810
Now, this worries me.

253
13:23.130 --> 13:24.610
- Let's go. - This way, Mr. Sarm.

254
13:26.810 --> 13:28.230
Lantao, look.

255
13:28.930 --> 13:30.330
Whoa...

256
13:31.910 --> 13:33.890
Hey, Lantao!

257
13:35.570 --> 13:36.730
Look at this.

258
13:37.410 --> 13:39.290
This eye thingy can move.

259
13:40.530 --> 13:41.290
Huh...

260
13:43.970 --> 13:45.170
Where did Lantao go?

261
13:49.730 --> 13:51.090
Where is he?

262
14:10.650 --> 14:11.490
Sarm.

263
14:11.850 --> 14:14.170
It's not proper to have me, Lady of Tani, being alone with you.

264
14:14.770 --> 14:17.330
Tell me who Toi-ting is.

265
14:18.390 --> 14:19.730
Why do I have to tell you, though?

266
14:20.250 --> 14:21.010
I'll give you 50,000.

267
14:23.530 --> 14:24.730
50,000 baht

268
14:25.050 --> 14:26.390
or 50,000 insults?

269
14:26.410 --> 14:27.530
50,000 baht.

270
14:27.590 --> 14:28.300
Now, who is it?

271
14:31.440 --> 14:33.090
Oh, It's that guy

272
14:33.890 --> 14:35.790
dressed up as a caveman spirit.

273
14:35.810 --> 14:37.330
That handsome guy.

274
14:39.170 --> 14:40.690
But not as handsome as you.

275
14:40.970 --> 14:41.890
Okay, then.

276
14:42.930 --> 14:43.650
Right.

277
14:44.090 --> 14:46.150
The one dressed up as The Flintstones?

278
14:46.170 --> 14:46.970
Yes.

279
14:47.810 --> 14:48.930
Orange costume.

280
14:49.410 --> 14:52.090
And do not tell Jam about this, okay?

281
14:52.810 --> 14:55.250
Though I look like this, I'm a spirit with good morals.

282
14:55.490 --> 14:57.090
Once the money is in my bank account,

283
14:57.250 --> 14:58.690
I'll keep my mouth shut.

284
14:59.810 --> 15:01.770
Oh...

285
15:02.120 --> 15:03.210
Oh, you.

286
15:04.400 --> 15:05.310
Umm, here.

287
15:05.330 --> 15:06.530
[Incoming Transfer: 50,000 baht]

288
15:07.010 --> 15:08.170
Thank you, Sarm.

289
15:08.810 --> 15:10.490
I hope you get to rule the world.

290
15:26.390 --> 15:27.890
What? Sarm?!

291
15:28.050 --> 15:29.130
Where did he go?!

292
15:33.410 --> 15:34.450
Sarm!

293
15:34.890 --> 15:36.250
Sarm!

294
15:54.850 --> 15:57.530
Good evening, Mr. Sarm. Are you interested in knocking some cans?

295
15:57.730 --> 15:58.490
Can you can a can?

296
15:59.770 --> 16:00.610
Just kidding.

297
16:01.330 --> 16:02.290
What are the prizes?

298
16:02.530 --> 16:04.490
The Charm Doll, the Enchanted Doll, and the Spellbound Doll.

299
16:04.510 --> 16:06.430
I'll take all the balls that you have.

300
16:06.450 --> 16:07.290
Sure.

301
16:07.530 --> 16:08.310
Wait a minute.

302
16:08.330 --> 16:09.290
I got here first.

303
16:09.730 --> 16:10.810
Did you pay, though?

304
16:13.270 --> 16:14.970
Just a kid in his twenties...?

305
16:15.530 --> 16:17.450
Will I be accused of bullying someone younger?

306
16:17.770 --> 16:18.410
Right.

307
16:19.090 --> 16:20.690
It wouldn't be wise to use my power.

308
16:21.050 --> 16:22.130
We'll share half of the balls we get, then.

309
16:22.190 --> 16:24.090
I'm good. Thank you.

310
16:25.500 --> 16:26.520
Whatever suits you.

311
16:29.330 --> 16:30.170
Can I have a ball, please?

312
16:30.850 --> 16:31.490
Here.

313
16:38.970 --> 16:40.250
Mr. Sarm.

314
16:40.650 --> 16:42.230
Which name should I engrave on the first doll?

315
16:42.250 --> 16:43.350
- Engraving a name? - A name.

316
16:43.370 --> 16:45.130
- Engraving a name? - A name is important.

317
16:47.310 --> 16:48.430
Is there a character limit?

318
16:48.450 --> 16:49.630
- No. - No limits either.

319
16:49.650 --> 16:50.330
Okay.

320
16:51.210 --> 16:52.530
Alright, for the the Charm Doll,

321
16:57.050 --> 16:58.450
let's do "Traiphop's Jiranat."

322
16:59.650 --> 17:00.870
How lovely.

323
17:00.890 --> 17:01.930
Of course.

324
17:11.930 --> 17:13.980
Mr. Sarm, and what about the Enchanted Doll?

325
17:13.990 --> 17:15.170
Oh, the Enchanted Doll, too.

326
17:16.329 --> 17:17.130
The Enchanted Doll.

327
17:17.329 --> 17:18.690
I went with our legal names... Oh, nicknames.

328
17:19.490 --> 17:23.410
Sarm belongs to Jam, XOXO, kiss, kiss, then.

329
17:23.569 --> 17:24.690
Very sweet.

330
17:25.450 --> 17:26.569
Of course.

331
17:39.290 --> 17:41.010
Oh, anything else?

332
17:41.050 --> 17:42.450
- That's all. - That's all?

333
17:42.610 --> 17:43.890
- We're doing this for real now. - Right.

334
17:48.210 --> 17:49.730
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

335
17:55.930 --> 17:57.430
- Awesome! - Well done, Mr. Sarm.

336
18:06.790 --> 18:07.610
Jam.

337
18:08.250 --> 18:09.690
There are blind boxes, too.

338
18:10.010 --> 18:11.290
There are ten boxes.

339
18:12.130 --> 18:13.730
Which one would you choose?

340
18:14.090 --> 18:15.510
The third one.

341
18:15.530 --> 18:18.050
Oh, the third one...

342
18:18.590 --> 18:20.050
Someone's madly in love.

343
18:32.010 --> 18:32.810
Okay.

344
18:35.010 --> 18:36.330
I got a devil horns headband.

345
18:40.430 --> 18:42.730
[Wasin: Come see me]

346
18:43.810 --> 18:44.690
Jam,

347
18:45.490 --> 18:47.730
I need to go see...

348
18:49.610 --> 18:50.970
Wasin now.

349
18:51.930 --> 18:53.670
Lantao...

350
18:53.690 --> 18:54.810
What really is going on?

351
18:54.830 --> 18:55.950
It's nothing.

352
18:55.970 --> 18:57.150
Are you sure?

353
18:57.170 --> 18:58.210
Yes.

354
18:58.450 --> 18:59.610
I'll see you in a bit.

355
19:00.180 --> 19:00.780
Mm.

356
19:07.830 --> 19:11.750
[Sarm: Where are you, my baby ghoul?]

357
19:11.770 --> 19:12.730
Sarm?

358
19:16.810 --> 19:17.730
Little Jam.

359
19:20.050 --> 19:20.970
Little Jam.

360
19:21.330 --> 19:22.210
What did you get?

361
19:22.450 --> 19:24.290
I just opened a blind box,

362
19:25.530 --> 19:26.890
and I got a devil horns headband.

363
19:27.930 --> 19:28.690
You don't like it?

364
19:29.310 --> 19:31.570
I prefer shaman prayer beads more.

365
19:32.290 --> 19:34.330
Okay, I'll buy you a prayer bead factory tomorrow.

366
19:34.890 --> 19:36.600
- That is crazy, Sarm. - Huh?

367
19:37.550 --> 19:38.770
And what about you?

368
19:39.210 --> 19:40.290
What did you get?

369
19:40.310 --> 19:41.010
These.

370
19:41.370 --> 19:43.170
I won a pair of dolls.

371
19:43.410 --> 19:44.810
They're the Charm Doll and the Enchanted Doll.

372
19:45.250 --> 19:46.650
What do you think? Aren't they adorable?

373
19:48.150 --> 19:49.810
Come on, look at him. This way.

374
19:51.030 --> 19:52.030
I think...

375
19:52.050 --> 19:53.820
I do not think they go well together.

376
19:54.890 --> 19:55.930
Just like us.

377
19:56.930 --> 19:58.290
Still, we worked it out, didn't we?

378
20:01.790 --> 20:02.690
Oh, hey.

379
20:03.390 --> 20:05.070
Remember the night we confessed our love?

380
20:06.150 --> 20:07.610
It is unforgettable.

381
20:09.090 --> 20:11.250
You were wearing a giant crab costume.

382
20:11.850 --> 20:13.810
The theme of the party was related to ghosts,

383
20:14.650 --> 20:16.810
yet you were the only one in a crab costume.

384
20:17.370 --> 20:18.090
What?

385
20:18.810 --> 20:19.970
There are crab spirits, you know?

386
20:20.450 --> 20:21.410
Like pervert ghost.

387
20:22.490 --> 20:23.730
Let me tell you something.

388
20:23.830 --> 20:25.330
This pervert ghost

389
20:25.630 --> 20:27.810
will haunt you

390
20:28.050 --> 20:29.410
forever.

391
20:30.170 --> 20:31.810
- Boo! - Hey, Sarm!

392
20:31.830 --> 20:32.760
You scared me.

393
20:32.770 --> 20:34.130
- Boo! - Hey!

394
20:35.450 --> 20:37.150
- Help me! - You want some of this?

395
20:37.170 --> 20:39.130
The pervert ghost is going to eat my liver!

396
20:41.090 --> 20:45.810
[Halloween with You]

397
21:03.450 --> 21:04.250
Why are you smiling?

398
21:05.830 --> 21:07.050
Today was so fun.

399
21:08.730 --> 21:09.850
When did you have the most fun?

400
21:12.270 --> 21:13.810
When you got jealous.

401
21:18.010 --> 21:19.370
Huh, I wasn't jealous.

402
21:25.890 --> 21:27.370
Oh...

403
21:30.730 --> 21:34.090
You were searching for Toi-ting throughout the whole event.

404
21:35.970 --> 21:37.330
Was that not being jealous?

405
21:42.200 --> 21:43.120
I was

406
21:43.690 --> 21:45.490
providing close protection.

407
21:51.690 --> 21:52.730
Sarm.

408
21:53.250 --> 21:53.970
Yes?

409
21:56.370 --> 21:58.630
What if someone flirted with you at the event?

410
21:59.380 --> 22:01.100
Oh, that's impossible.

411
22:02.490 --> 22:04.010
What if it happened?

412
22:06.930 --> 22:08.410
I'd say that I already have a spouse.

413
22:09.850 --> 22:11.210
And he's extremely adorable, too.

414
22:13.010 --> 22:13.810
And that...

415
22:15.010 --> 22:16.330
I really do love him.

416
22:18.130 --> 22:19.410
You have a good way with words.

417
22:21.650 --> 22:22.290
Hey.

418
22:22.770 --> 22:23.410
Hm?

419
22:25.210 --> 22:27.810
Can I give you a scrub bath tonight, my dear?

420
22:33.090 --> 22:33.970
Would that cost anything?

421
22:34.140 --> 22:35.180
It's free for life.

422
22:36.070 --> 22:37.170
No strings attached.

423
23:07.890 --> 23:08.970
Shall we begin?

424
23:13.050 --> 23:14.170
Let's get it done and head to bed quickly.

425
23:16.130 --> 23:17.090
Why?

426
23:17.790 --> 23:18.890
I have to wake up early tomorrow.

427
23:24.410 --> 23:26.490
How about we stay up the whole night, then?

428
23:41.410 --> 23:42.130
Oh.

429
23:51.090 --> 23:52.450
Are those my glasses?

430
24:07.490 --> 24:08.470
And...

431
24:09.690 --> 24:11.570
Where are they, then?

432
24:15.770 --> 24:17.130
Are they right here?

433
24:22.970 --> 24:23.930
Let's get it on, then.

434
24:31.090 --> 24:32.350
Your migraine pills?

435
24:32.370 --> 24:33.270
Always with me.

436
24:33.290 --> 24:34.270
Your shaving kit?

437
24:34.290 --> 24:35.290
Already in the luggage.

438
24:35.490 --> 24:36.790
Leg warmers?

439
24:36.810 --> 24:37.810
Sunglasses?

440
24:37.910 --> 24:38.750
Belts?

441
24:38.770 --> 24:39.610
Lotions?

442
24:40.770 --> 24:42.290
My spouse has already taken care of them.

443
24:43.090 --> 24:44.970
I didn't forget anything, my dear.

444
24:45.130 --> 24:45.930
You did.

445
24:46.890 --> 24:47.690
What is it?

446
24:48.130 --> 24:48.690
Huh?

447
24:48.850 --> 24:50.450
You forgot to kiss me.

448
24:55.590 --> 24:56.410
Ow...

449
24:58.450 --> 24:59.170
Hey.

450
24:59.850 --> 25:00.670
While I'm away,

451
25:00.690 --> 25:02.530
do not wander off on your own, okay?

452
25:03.650 --> 25:05.450
I will not wander off on my own.

453
25:08.050 --> 25:09.810
I will go with Lantao.

454
25:10.530 --> 25:11.250
No.

455
25:13.090 --> 25:13.770
Don't do that.

456
25:14.900 --> 25:16.380
Don't forget to eat, too.

457
25:17.210 --> 25:18.590
I've already told Mod-dang

458
25:18.610 --> 25:20.130
to prepare food for you.

459
25:20.370 --> 25:22.250
Every meal, every day.

460
25:22.410 --> 25:23.730
That is too much, Sarm.

461
25:24.150 --> 25:26.130
Hey, if nobody prepares food for you,

462
25:26.670 --> 25:28.290
you'll sneak out to have junk food.

463
25:28.590 --> 25:29.750
Mm...

464
25:30.250 --> 25:31.810
I will stay fed. Don't worry.

465
25:32.850 --> 25:33.890
On top of that,

466
25:35.150 --> 25:37.130
don't overwork yourself.

467
25:37.310 --> 25:39.870
If I catch you doing it again,

468
25:39.890 --> 25:40.570
we'll see about that!

469
25:42.450 --> 25:43.370
Understood?

470
25:46.570 --> 25:47.730
What will you do to me?

471
25:48.410 --> 25:49.090
Hm?

472
25:49.610 --> 25:50.410
I will...

473
25:53.890 --> 25:55.550
ask you to take it easy.

474
25:55.570 --> 25:56.690
All you do is work.

475
25:57.490 --> 25:58.290
I'm worried about you.

476
25:59.710 --> 26:00.610
Understood?

477
26:02.010 --> 26:03.370
One last thing.

478
26:04.170 --> 26:05.090
Don't...

479
26:05.410 --> 26:06.770
forget to miss me.

480
26:09.930 --> 26:11.250
Same to you, Sarm.

481
26:12.210 --> 26:13.810
Eat well, okay?

482
26:14.570 --> 26:15.370
Absolutely.

483
26:17.090 --> 26:18.290
Should I get you some treats from there?

484
26:18.810 --> 26:20.250
I am not a kid.

485
26:20.770 --> 26:21.510
Hey.

486
26:22.690 --> 26:23.890
I'll be away only for two weeks.

487
26:24.290 --> 26:25.250
I'll be back in a flash.

488
26:28.450 --> 26:29.810
Take good care of Little Jam, okay?

489
26:29.890 --> 26:31.030
If something happens to him,

490
26:31.050 --> 26:32.130
I won't let it slide.

491
26:32.370 --> 26:33.410
- Yes, Boss. - Huh.

492
26:33.610 --> 26:34.850
I can lose anything,

493
26:35.570 --> 26:36.610
but not you, Little Jam,

494
26:36.690 --> 26:37.850
I can't lose you.

495
26:38.390 --> 26:40.570
No thief is coming to steal me.

496
26:40.610 --> 26:42.370
Well, I care about what's mine.

497
26:43.930 --> 26:44.850
I'll be going now.

498
26:48.370 --> 26:49.170
Bye-bye.

499
26:49.970 --> 26:51.130
Bye-bye.

500
26:54.010 --> 26:54.810
See you.

501
26:55.090 --> 26:55.890
Bye-bye.

502
26:57.090 --> 26:58.090
Bye-bye.

503
26:59.070 --> 27:00.490
Take care of yourself.

504
27:10.570 --> 27:11.490
Bye-bye.

505
27:20.470 --> 27:21.210
Wait!

506
27:21.930 --> 27:22.690
I'm right here.

507
27:24.510 --> 27:25.290
What?

508
27:25.650 --> 27:26.490
Huh?

509
27:27.250 --> 27:28.290
Sarm?!

510
27:29.250 --> 27:30.750
Why did you not hop on the car?

511
27:30.770 --> 27:31.930
It left before I could.

512
27:32.090 --> 27:32.990
I'll be seeing you.

513
27:33.210 --> 27:34.450
Bye-bye, Little Jam.

514
27:34.830 --> 27:35.690
Miss you.

515
27:36.110 --> 27:37.930
- Bye-bye. - Don't forget to miss me, too!

516
27:38.490 --> 27:39.230
Bye-bye.

517
27:39.250 --> 27:40.450
Bye-bye.

518
27:40.730 --> 27:41.930
Hey, back up the car right now.

519
27:42.130 --> 27:43.290
Should I fire you?

520
27:44.810 --> 27:47.650
[One week later]

521
27:55.280 --> 27:57.370
Simply follow the plans that have been laid out.

522
27:58.390 --> 27:59.390
Thank you very much.

523
27:59.690 --> 28:01.030
[Sarm: Miss you, babe]

524
28:01.040 --> 28:05.360
[Sarm: I need your love. I don't have the energy to work]

525
28:10.610 --> 28:11.970
Okay.

526
28:12.670 --> 28:14.750
Thank you. [Sarm: Has your work been draining?]

527
28:14.770 --> 28:17.910
[Sarm: Don't forget to eat]

528
28:17.930 --> 28:19.790
[Day 8]

529
28:19.810 --> 28:21.770
Would you like to have any menu in particular?

530
28:22.370 --> 28:24.450
Anything will do, Dad.

531
28:25.670 --> 28:26.490
Nim,

532
28:26.500 --> 28:28.410
- Yes? - serve him a dish of anything.

533
28:28.610 --> 28:30.430
Understood. I'll get it ready soon.

534
28:30.450 --> 28:31.240
Mm, wait.

535
28:31.260 --> 28:32.050
You know what to get?

536
28:33.850 --> 28:36.050
- I'll have a look in the kitchen. - Okay.

537
28:37.810 --> 28:40.090
How are you? How is your work here?

538
28:40.370 --> 28:41.450
It has been great,

539
28:41.850 --> 28:43.810
I am still settling in.

540
28:45.650 --> 28:47.890
Okay. Here, let's settle in.

541
28:50.730 --> 28:52.090
Welcome.

542
28:52.490 --> 28:53.870
Thank you.

543
28:58.250 --> 28:59.510
[Day 11]

544
28:59.530 --> 29:01.130
Jam, can you help me with this?

545
29:01.410 --> 29:03.150
I'm thinking of buying this collection of clothes,

546
29:03.170 --> 29:04.670
and I trust your sense of fashion.

547
29:04.690 --> 29:07.130
Can you pick the one you like?

548
29:08.110 --> 29:09.410
Whoa.

549
29:10.410 --> 29:11.930
I think these are all beautiful.

550
29:12.330 --> 29:14.250
Mm, this crop top looks...

551
29:14.570 --> 29:15.530
interesting.

552
29:15.770 --> 29:16.730
What do you think?

553
29:17.150 --> 29:17.890
Is it a wonderful pick?

554
29:18.810 --> 29:19.970
I think it is.

555
29:20.330 --> 29:23.530
I have never seen you

556
29:23.850 --> 29:25.850
in an outfit this sexy before.

557
29:26.530 --> 29:28.310
I never have the guts to wear one.

558
29:28.330 --> 29:30.390
You would look fantastic in any of these.

559
29:30.410 --> 29:32.170
Oh, are you telling a white lie?

560
29:32.470 --> 29:34.390
I am not. Well...

561
29:34.810 --> 29:37.110
Just look at your body and everything.

562
29:37.130 --> 29:38.990
- Nonsense... - They all look good.

563
29:39.010 --> 29:40.290
You're flattering me, Jam.

564
29:40.750 --> 29:42.910
How about we wear matching outfits instead?

565
29:44.090 --> 29:45.550
I'm going to wear the crop top,

566
29:45.570 --> 29:46.890
and you might wear

567
29:46.950 --> 29:49.030
some cute cardigan.

568
29:49.050 --> 29:50.330
But both with the same pattern.

569
29:50.690 --> 29:52.790
- Mm. - Right? It's a lovely idea, isn't it?

570
29:53.410 --> 29:54.990
Then we might also...

571
29:55.010 --> 29:57.250
take some photos and show them to Sarm.

572
29:59.770 --> 30:01.250
I think it is a good idea.

573
30:03.250 --> 30:05.250
I believe this one really suits you.

574
30:12.970 --> 30:14.730
This one also looks interesting.

575
30:20.330 --> 30:21.250
Jam.

576
30:22.390 --> 30:23.330
Jam.

577
30:24.550 --> 30:25.810
- Jam! - Yes?

578
30:27.350 --> 30:28.770
You miss him, don't you?

579
30:31.570 --> 30:32.970
Who are you referring to, Song?

580
30:33.030 --> 30:33.670
There.

581
30:34.530 --> 30:35.970
I can see right through you.

582
30:36.410 --> 30:38.330
Who am I missing? No...no one.

583
30:38.350 --> 30:40.630
- Song. - Stop pretending, Jam.

584
30:40.650 --> 30:41.690
The eyes

585
30:41.890 --> 30:43.410
never lie.

586
30:45.110 --> 30:46.770
I am closing my eyes, then.

587
30:48.130 --> 30:50.410
So you are flustered. Are you admitting to that?

588
30:51.170 --> 30:52.290
Ow...

589
30:52.430 --> 30:54.510
Stop teasing me, Song.

590
30:54.530 --> 30:56.650
I get it. You two are far apart.

591
30:57.690 --> 30:59.730
It's normal to miss your partner.

592
31:01.790 --> 31:03.070
There. You're blushing again.

593
31:04.290 --> 31:05.790
Aw, you're blushing so much.

594
31:05.810 --> 31:07.690
Even your ears are now red, too.

595
31:08.170 --> 31:09.550
You miss him that much, don't you?

596
31:09.570 --> 31:11.090
Come on, Song.

597
31:11.490 --> 31:12.890
- Oh, your cheeks are red. - Oh.

598
31:12.930 --> 31:14.330
I will tease you back.

599
31:15.650 --> 31:17.550
Once you have a partner,

600
31:17.570 --> 31:19.130
I will tease you every day.

601
31:19.290 --> 31:20.490
Go ahead, then.

602
31:21.490 --> 31:22.650
[Day 13]

603
31:22.670 --> 31:23.950
[Sarm: What are you doing?]

604
31:23.970 --> 31:25.390
[Sarm: Miss you, babe]

605
31:25.410 --> 31:26.680
[Jam: Do you?]

606
31:27.370 --> 31:28.530
I cannot wait.

607
31:57.570 --> 31:58.530
Sarm!

608
31:59.290 --> 31:59.930
Babe.

609
32:00.370 --> 32:01.330
I'm home.

610
32:06.970 --> 32:08.050
I missed you so much.

611
32:14.730 --> 32:15.890
Are you tired?

612
32:21.970 --> 32:23.490
There.

613
32:34.850 --> 32:35.970
It's been too long.

614
32:40.070 --> 32:41.730
You were away for two weeks.

615
32:44.210 --> 32:45.370
Are you tired?

616
32:46.650 --> 32:47.650
Are you?

617
32:50.290 --> 32:51.450
I missed you more than anything.

618
32:53.230 --> 32:54.330
These past two weeks,

619
32:54.790 --> 32:55.970
I'd been missing you a lot.

620
32:57.010 --> 32:57.850
I missed you so much.

621
32:58.270 --> 32:59.130
I really did.

622
33:00.170 --> 33:00.890
So very much.

623
33:34.650 --> 33:36.890
I missed you a lot, too.

624
33:46.130 --> 33:47.170
How much do you miss me,

625
33:52.850 --> 33:54.290
- huh? - Very much.

626
33:56.570 --> 33:57.770
This much.

627
33:59.930 --> 34:01.010
I missed this

628
34:02.450 --> 34:03.370
and this.

629
34:04.850 --> 34:05.710
And this.

630
34:05.730 --> 34:06.530
This, too.

631
34:07.110 --> 34:08.050
- Also this. - Ow.

632
34:08.250 --> 34:08.949
This, too.

633
34:08.969 --> 34:10.170
Ow.

634
34:21.690 --> 34:22.889
I missed this voice.

635
34:23.170 --> 34:24.330
I missed everything.

636
34:53.290 --> 34:54.570
If that is the case,

637
34:56.630 --> 35:00.130
go ahead and knock yourself out tonight.

638
35:04.730 --> 35:05.570
Don't mind if I do.

639
35:24.310 --> 35:26.610
Please do not be away for this long again.

640
35:30.010 --> 35:31.010
If I could choose,

641
35:31.490 --> 35:32.530
I'd never want to go anywhere.

642
35:33.050 --> 35:34.410
I'd never want to be away from you.

643
35:41.350 --> 35:42.730
What about the meetings?

644
35:43.330 --> 35:44.530
Online meetings exist,

645
35:46.570 --> 35:47.530
right?

646
35:55.610 --> 35:58.290
I really missed you, you know?

647
36:01.330 --> 36:02.490
So did I.

648
36:03.850 --> 36:05.370
No matter how far apart we are,

649
36:05.930 --> 36:08.410
my house is always right here.

650
36:08.890 --> 36:09.730
Right here.

651
36:10.010 --> 36:10.810
And here.

652
36:11.170 --> 36:12.090
Here, too.

653
36:42.890 --> 36:43.810
Are you hungry?

654
36:44.810 --> 36:46.490
I am still full, actually.

655
36:46.630 --> 36:47.730
Tell me if you're hungry, then.

656
36:48.690 --> 36:51.450
You will take me to a restaurant, right?

657
36:51.650 --> 36:52.570
No.

658
36:53.330 --> 36:54.450
I'll stop the car,

659
36:54.610 --> 36:56.850
and you'll have to jump into the water

660
36:57.070 --> 36:58.010
and catch some fish yourself.

661
36:59.770 --> 37:01.790
You are messing with me again, Sarm.

662
37:01.810 --> 37:02.850
Just kidding.

663
37:03.130 --> 37:05.150
I made you sandwiches.

664
37:05.170 --> 37:06.650
And I got you pomegranate juice.

665
37:07.610 --> 37:08.850
They're in the back.

666
37:12.530 --> 37:13.730
How lovely.

667
37:14.950 --> 37:16.570
Then love me a whole bunch.

668
37:18.410 --> 37:19.930
I already do.

669
37:20.730 --> 37:21.850
You love me a lot,

670
37:22.370 --> 37:24.010
then you have to spoil me a bunch, too.

671
37:27.530 --> 37:29.690
You are being clingy.

672
37:29.930 --> 37:31.310
You have something in mind, do you not?

673
37:31.330 --> 37:32.250
You caught me.

674
37:32.850 --> 37:33.810
Well...

675
37:36.770 --> 37:37.850
Do you know that

676
37:39.330 --> 37:40.490
a good spouse

677
37:41.710 --> 37:42.850
is the one...

678
37:43.370 --> 37:45.490
who wears a fluffy tail?

679
37:46.790 --> 37:47.930
A lovely

680
37:47.950 --> 37:48.930
and fluffy tail.

681
37:52.610 --> 37:54.610
And do you know this?

682
37:55.130 --> 37:55.730
Yes?

683
37:55.910 --> 37:58.090
Do you know that a good spouse for me...

684
37:58.390 --> 37:59.200
What is it?

685
37:59.470 --> 38:00.690
is a new spouse entirely?

686
38:02.450 --> 38:04.570
Oh, Little Jam.

687
38:05.650 --> 38:06.850
I was joking.

688
38:08.420 --> 38:09.750
I just want to entertain my spouse.

689
38:10.140 --> 38:10.940
So that tonight

690
38:14.100 --> 38:15.740
you'll have to entertain me in return.

691
38:16.700 --> 38:18.140
Sarm.

692
38:18.920 --> 38:21.620
Oh, you slapped me, too?

693
38:22.500 --> 38:26.040
You always find ways to come back to that topic.

694
38:26.060 --> 38:29.180
Just want to be clingy with you...

695
38:29.440 --> 38:30.820
Let us hit the road.

696
38:30.860 --> 38:32.780
- Find. - Are you heading out or not?

697
38:32.860 --> 38:34.620
Sure, let's head out.

698
39:01.530 --> 39:02.690
Sarm...

699
39:32.790 --> 39:33.840
Sarm?

700
39:38.670 --> 39:40.090
Oh, Sarm.

701
39:40.110 --> 39:41.390
Ta-da!

702
39:41.750 --> 39:43.490
I bought a bunch of crabs for you.

703
39:43.510 --> 39:44.190
Look, look.

704
39:50.710 --> 39:51.890
You were sleeping,

705
39:51.910 --> 39:52.910
so I didn't want to wake you up.

706
39:52.930 --> 39:53.790
Feeling hungry?

707
40:00.870 --> 40:02.770
I want to go for a stroll.

708
40:02.790 --> 40:03.870
Then, let's go.

709
40:04.090 --> 40:04.710
Come on.

710
40:05.230 --> 40:05.830
Alright.

711
40:08.230 --> 40:08.950
Let us go.

712
40:25.130 --> 40:26.750
Sarm, do you remember that

713
40:28.390 --> 40:31.670
you climbed up a coconut tree because some kids dared you to?

714
40:32.590 --> 40:34.230
Who would forget their own achievements?

715
40:39.270 --> 40:42.110
You gave me a lot of headaches back then.

716
40:45.070 --> 40:45.670
But...

717
40:46.390 --> 40:47.550
If it wasn't for that day,

718
40:48.910 --> 40:50.210
we wouldn't end up together like this.

719
40:55.650 --> 40:56.590
For many things that have happened,

720
40:58.230 --> 40:59.630
after looking back at them,

721
41:01.290 --> 41:03.290
there's a lot that I'm grateful for.

722
41:06.790 --> 41:07.950
I want to thank you

723
41:08.670 --> 41:09.950
for helping me to be here.

724
41:17.630 --> 41:19.030
Because you're more than just love.

725
41:22.510 --> 41:23.870
You're the other half of me.

726
41:27.710 --> 41:28.710
You're my other half,

727
41:30.830 --> 41:31.750
my thinking partner,

728
41:34.790 --> 41:36.070
and my support.

729
41:43.090 --> 41:44.230
I love you, Little Jam.

730
41:46.790 --> 41:47.750
I really do.

731
41:55.110 --> 41:57.070
I love you, too, Sarm.

732
42:00.150 --> 42:01.550
I love you more than anyone else.

733
42:03.110 --> 42:04.350
When do you love me the most?

734
42:08.350 --> 42:10.960
When you're aware of your own surroundings.

735
42:13.110 --> 42:14.640
That almost ended on a positive note.

736
42:25.950 --> 42:27.390
I never thought that

737
42:28.070 --> 42:30.630
someone who I fought to the death with

738
42:35.190 --> 42:37.030
would become my soulmate.

739
42:41.390 --> 42:43.110
Now and forever,

740
42:46.590 --> 42:48.710
I want you to be a part of my life.

741
42:54.010 --> 42:56.180
The one who can be at my side

742
42:57.490 --> 42:58.790
can be no one else

743
42:59.790 --> 43:00.710
but you...

744
43:02.270 --> 43:03.190
Jiranat.

745
43:26.970 --> 43:27.470
Oh.

746
43:28.070 --> 43:28.990
Little Jam.

747
43:29.230 --> 43:30.870
- Yes? - No, come here.

748
43:31.310 --> 43:32.990
This is very wrong.

749
43:34.390 --> 43:35.070
Here.

750
43:41.590 --> 43:44.360
You're adorable, so you can have another bite.

751
43:45.230 --> 43:47.350
Oh, it's on your lips.

752
43:56.190 --> 43:57.190
All clean now.

753
43:58.840 --> 44:00.920
- You take care of me so well. - Of course.

754
44:02.710 --> 44:04.430
We have finally made it back home, have we not?

755
44:06.290 --> 44:06.950
Yeah.

756
44:07.190 --> 44:07.830
But

757
44:08.430 --> 44:10.350
I don't know why I can still smell the sea.

758
44:11.790 --> 44:13.750
You are always being so extra.

759
44:17.050 --> 44:18.270
So extra.

760
44:18.870 --> 44:19.950
Eat up.

761
44:20.150 --> 44:21.470
Or else you'll miss

762
44:21.700 --> 44:23.560
these tasty treats when you're back to work.

763
44:28.630 --> 44:29.950
I think...

764
44:30.340 --> 44:32.760
I miss the one who cooks for me more.

765
44:33.810 --> 44:34.910
You mean the chef?

766
44:40.200 --> 44:41.240
- Yes. - Oh.

767
44:42.630 --> 44:43.590
Lucky you,

768
44:44.470 --> 44:45.510
because that handsome chef

769
44:46.390 --> 44:47.520
is your spouse.

770
44:50.230 --> 44:51.570
You are so full of yourself.

771
44:51.590 --> 44:52.350
Always.

772
44:57.930 --> 44:59.350
Back to eating.

773
45:00.470 --> 45:01.670
Let me feed you, too.

774
45:03.100 --> 45:04.610
Alright...

775
45:04.970 --> 45:06.430
Sarm, open wide.

776
45:11.710 --> 45:12.630
Is it sweet?

777
45:13.950 --> 45:14.790
It is,

778
45:15.490 --> 45:16.670
but not as sweet as your lips.

779
45:21.740 --> 45:22.980
It is a shame that

780
45:23.550 --> 45:25.070
the trip is over.

781
45:26.110 --> 45:26.830
Hey,

782
45:27.750 --> 45:29.390
our story isn't over, though.

783
45:30.150 --> 45:30.790
Mm.

784
45:32.120 --> 45:33.500
I have to wake up early

785
45:35.110 --> 45:36.150
to go to work

786
45:36.850 --> 45:37.710
and go to meetings.

787
45:39.150 --> 45:40.150
It's as exhausting as always.

788
45:42.030 --> 45:44.230
But you will get to come home and have dinner with me.

789
45:46.030 --> 45:47.470
And fight over a blanket.

790
45:48.290 --> 45:49.640
You stole my blanket.

791
45:49.770 --> 45:50.840
That's incorrect.

792
45:50.860 --> 45:51.610
Am I wrong?

793
45:54.110 --> 45:55.550
I just wanted to hug you.

794
46:16.730 --> 46:18.510
Thank you, Sarm.

795
46:20.870 --> 46:22.030
For what?

796
46:25.270 --> 46:27.990
For turning ordinary days

797
46:30.290 --> 46:31.950
into memorable ones.

798
46:45.030 --> 46:45.670
Hey.

799
46:48.070 --> 46:49.310
Promise me one thing.

800
46:52.830 --> 46:53.910
What is it?

801
46:56.830 --> 46:57.830
No matter how sad,

802
46:59.750 --> 47:00.550
how happy,

803
47:03.510 --> 47:04.550
how upset,

804
47:06.070 --> 47:07.750
how tired you are or how much you cry,

805
47:11.290 --> 47:12.950
you have to come home and have dinner with me.

806
47:17.670 --> 47:18.830
I promise you,

807
47:20.470 --> 47:21.790
my spouse.

808
47:25.470 --> 47:26.350
You're the best.

809
47:29.230 --> 47:30.310
Back then,

810
47:30.950 --> 47:32.670
I once believed that love

811
47:33.070 --> 47:35.270
meant searching for the perfect person,

812
47:35.410 --> 47:37.410
but only through living my own life

813
47:38.990 --> 47:40.590
have I realized that...

814
47:40.910 --> 47:44.230
love means being with someone who accepts our flaws

815
47:44.830 --> 47:47.110
and chooses to hold our hand every single day.

816
47:48.890 --> 47:50.550
I'm not the most talented man in the world.

817
47:51.210 --> 47:52.750
My words aren't always sweet.

818
47:53.190 --> 47:54.550
And I often make mistakes.

819
47:55.990 --> 47:57.590
But whenever I turn around,

820
47:57.910 --> 47:59.150
I'm always happy to see that

821
47:59.570 --> 48:01.230
the person next to me is still Jam.

822
48:02.210 --> 48:04.210
We have been through the days we fought,

823
48:07.860 --> 48:09.440
the days we longed for one another,

824
48:09.800 --> 48:11.280
and the days we had to be apart.

825
48:13.320 --> 48:14.920
We pushed through and persevered.

826
48:15.670 --> 48:17.270
Because we never let go of each other's hands.

827
48:18.390 --> 48:21.590
What is the best part of my life?

828
48:27.510 --> 48:29.130
My answer would be...

829
48:29.710 --> 48:31.870
- the days I have you by my side. - The days I have you by my side.

830
48:32.870 --> 48:35.430
The story of Traiphop and Jiranat

831
48:36.080 --> 48:37.800
may have ended here,

832
48:38.950 --> 48:40.630
but our love story

833
48:40.950 --> 48:42.070
has only just begun.

